        "original_id": "29d5eefd-9a7a-5d6d-abaa-3f5bef4d7acb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Terry Kath, Róisín Murphy, Mark Brydon, Matthew Herbert\n- Organizations: Chicago, Moloko\n- Products: Ruby Blue, “Sow into You”\n- Topics: rock, trip hop, electronica\n\nFacts:\n- Terry Kath was born on January 31, 1946, and he died on January 23, 1978.\n- Terry Kath was an American musician and songwriter who was the original guitarist, one of the lead singers, and a founding member of the rock band Chicago.\n- Róisín Murphy was born on July 5, 1973, and she is an Irish singer-songwriter and record producer.\n- In the 1990s, Róisín Murphy first became known as one-half of the UK trip hop duo Moloko with her partner Mark Brydon.\n- In 2005, Róisín Murphy and Matthew Herbert wrote and produced the electronica song “Sow into You” for Murphy’s debut solo album Ruby Blue.",
